lldb-dap on Windows: neutralize LLDB_API so inline members are usable.

The SB API headers default LLDB_API to __declspec(dllimport) for any
Windows consumer that is not the DLL itself. dllimport is prescriptive:
it forbids using a member's inline definition and demands an import --
and members like SBCommand's implicit destructor and Status::takeError
exist ONLY inline, so under -O2 no object ever defines them and the
import cannot be satisfied. Mach-O never meets this: visibility
annotations are additive, which is why the Mac tree builds lldb-dap
with no change here.

Defining LLDB_API empty (the headers guard with #ifndef) lets lldb-dap
compile inline members inline; every out-of-line symbol still resolves
through the DLL's import library, which provides thunks for functions
with no annotation needed.

--- a/utils/bazel/llvm-project-overlay/lldb/BUILD.bazel
+++ b/utils/bazel/llvm-project-overlay/lldb/BUILD.bazel
@@ -1302,9 +1302,16 @@
 cc_binary(
     name = "lldb-dap",
     srcs = glob([
         "tools/lldb-dap/**/*.cpp",
         "tools/lldb-dap/**/*.h",
     ]),
+    local_defines = select({
+        "@platforms//os:windows": [
+            "LLDB_API=",
+            "LLDB_PRIVATE_EXPORT=",
+        ],
+        "//conditions:default": [],
+    }),
     additional_linker_inputs = [
         ":lldb-dap-plist",
     ],
